=== ISSUE ===
Title: get_team_members ignores its max: Lichess has no max parameter, so the tool reads the whole member list

`GET /api/team/{teamId}/users` has no `max` parameter in the Lichess API spec (https://github.com/lichess-org/api/blob/906d1a6e93ca1ba4b65c9decb3077f2431c6d55a/doc/specs/lichess-api.yaml); it streams every member as NDJSON. Live, `max=2` on lichess-swiss streamed 250 members in 5 seconds and kept going. The tool sends `?max=` and reads the whole stream, so for a big team it downloads and returns the full member list.

=== PR ===
Title: fix: get_team_members stops reading after max members
Body:
Closes #<issue>

- Adds `parseNdjsonUpTo(response, max)` in `src/http/parse.ts`: reads NDJSON incrementally, stops at `max`, and cancels the body.
- `get_team_members` uses it and no longer sends the ignored `max`.

Spec: https://github.com/lichess-org/api/blob/906d1a6e93ca1ba4b65c9decb3077f2431c6d55a/doc/specs/lichess-api.yaml

Commits: tests first (5 fail), then the fix.
Verification: 365/365 tests pass. Live: 3 members from lichess-swiss in about 400ms.
